{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Spent the remaining allocation on the one thread whose account was still source-only: the StateSnapshot repair duty. The harness forces a follower's Progress into StateSnapshot on a real leader by compacting storage past the follower's next index with a snapshot present and the peer recently active, entering that state through the production call maybeSendAppend, and then exercises both producers named in the source account. A local run records the entry state (StateSnapshot, match 1, PendingSnapshot 2, paused true, one message emitted) and then: a peer MsgAppResp reporting index 2 leaves the Progress in StateReplicate with match 2 and unpaused, while an application snapshot report delivered as a rejecting MsgSnapStatus leaves a freshly snapshotted Progress in StateProbe with PendingSnapshot cleared to 0 and appends still paused. Submitted as a fixed experiment for investigation a38031973bee49ac9248ded78a2843e4-question-1, with scope, prefix, two prerequisites and two comparisons (state_after StateReplicate and state_after StateProbe) plus the existing behaviour fact as a knowledge use, so the controller can produce the receipt; no interpretation is added because that receipt does not exist yet, and it explicitly excludes the case where the MsgAppResp is lost entirely, which stays a source-based account. The two asserted defects and their receipts are unchanged.\"}"}}
